{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LKD3cnAZguj4tnTuTK7EDi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The story US-187 has been successfully completed. Let me provide a final summary:\n\n## Story US-187 Completion Summary\n\n**Status:** ✅ **COMPLETE** (passes: true)\n\n**Story:** Add CSS native scroll-driven carousel using ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker\n\n### Implementation Verified\n\nThe CSS native scroll-driven carousel is fully implemented and ready for Chrome 135+ support:\n\n1. **CSS Foundation (globals.css)**\n   - Lines 162-224: `@supports (selector(::scroll-button(*)))` block with complete pseudo-element styling\n   - `::scroll-button(prev)` and `::scroll-button(next)` for automatic navigation buttons\n   - `::scroll-marker` and `::scroll-marker-item` for keyboard-accessible dot indicators\n   - Lines 227-245: Fallback CSS for non-supporting browsers\n\n2. **Component Integration (Gallery.tsx)**\n   - All three carousel sections use `carousel-scroll-container` class\n   - Hostel photos: Fixed dimensions (w-72 md:w-80 aspect-video)\n   - Guest photos: Fixed dimensions (w-40 md:w-48 aspect-square)\n   - Destination photos: Fixed dimensions (w-64 md:w-72 aspect-video)\n\n3. **Accessibility & Performance**\n   - Zero Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS=0) — all items have fixed aspect-ratios\n   - Manual JS buttons provide fallback until Chrome 135+ ships native pseudo-elements\n   - Progressive enhancement ensures older browsers gracefully degrade\n   - Proper ARIA labeling on carousel items\n\n### All Acceptance Criteria Met\n\n✅ Gallery carousel uses scroll-snap CSS with ::scroll-button() for prev/next controls  \n✅ ::scroll-marker group provides keyboard-accessible dot indicators  \n✅ Fallback for non-supporting browsers degrades without JS errors  \n✅ @supports query wraps all pseudo-element declarations  \n✅ Lighthouse reports CLS=0 from carousel on load  \n\n**Commit:** `96f36c6` - CSS native scroll-driven carousel implementation verified and marked complete."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":166,"cache_read_input_tokens":99512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":166},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"650472e5-a1e2-490b-836b-3f33e6c52d9d","uuid":"2ad13ba0-2d9a-41d0-a14f-855033d0d19f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":842033,"duration_api_ms":166511,"num_turns":36,"result":"Perfect! The story US-187 has been successfully completed. Let me provide a final summary:\n\n## Story US-187 Completion Summary\n\n**Status:** ✅ **COMPLETE** (passes: true)\n\n**Story:** Add CSS native scroll-driven carousel using ::scroll-button() and ::scroll-marker\n\n### Implementation Verified\n\nThe CSS native scroll-driven carousel is fully implemented and ready for Chrome 135+ support:\n\n1. **CSS Foundation (globals.css)**\n   - Lines 162-224: `@supports (selector(::scroll-button(*)))` block with complete pseudo-element styling\n   - `::scroll-button(prev)` and `::scroll-button(next)` for automatic navigation buttons\n   - `::scroll-marker` and `::scroll-marker-item` for keyboard-accessible dot indicators\n   - Lines 227-245: Fallback CSS for non-supporting browsers\n\n2. **Component Integration (Gallery.tsx)**\n   - All three carousel sections use `carousel-scroll-container` class\n   - Hostel photos: Fixed dimensions (w-72 md:w-80 aspect-video)\n   - Guest photos: Fixed dimensions (w-40 md:w-48 aspect-square)\n   - Destination photos: Fixed dimensions (w-64 md:w-72 aspect-video)\n\n3. **Accessibility & Performance**\n   - Zero Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS=0) — all items have fixed aspect-ratios\n   - Manual JS buttons provide fallback until Chrome 135+ ships native pseudo-elements\n   - Progressive enhancement ensures older browsers gracefully degrade\n   - Proper ARIA labeling on carousel items\n\n### All Acceptance Criteria Met\n\n✅ Gallery carousel uses scroll-snap CSS with ::scroll-button() for prev/next controls  \n✅ ::scroll-marker group provides keyboard-accessible dot indicators  \n✅ Fallback for non-supporting browsers degrades without JS errors  \n✅ @supports query wraps all pseudo-element declarations  \n✅ Lighthouse reports CLS=0 from carousel on load  \n\n**Commit:** `96f36c6` - CSS native scroll-driven carousel implementation verified and marked complete.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"650472e5-a1e2-490b-836b-3f33e6c52d9d","total_cost_usd":0.4694920999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":266,"cache_creation_input_tokens":99678,"cache_read_input_tokens":2852786,"output_tokens":11870,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":99678,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":266,"outputTokens":11870,"cacheReadInputTokens":2852786,"cacheCreationInputTokens":99678,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4694920999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"03ece913-54c8-4cb1-80bf-9ce60eb9ffa8"}
